translit for OS-9/68000=======================ORIG holds comp.sources.misc volume 36, translit 1.0 (ten parts), asposted -- the whole package, which its terms require to travel together:source, tables, documentation, examples and the order form.  The filesbeside it build the OS-9 program.What changed, and why:  paths.h     Under OSK the tables are looked for in /dd/LIB/translit/              when they are not in the current directory, and GETOPT is 0,              so translit uses the getopt() it carries; the default              libraries have none.  translit.c  The tables name the end of a line as \0x0A, the Unix newline,              and an OS-9 text line ends in 0x0D, so no end-of-line rule              ever matched (koi8-tex.rus dropped every `\\').  Under OSK              input 0x0D is read as 0x0A and output 0x0A is written as 0x0D              -- tl_getc(), tl_putc() and tl_puts() -- so every table works              as posted.  A genuine 0x0A byte in the input comes out as              0x0D.reg_exp.c, reg_sub.c and reg_exp.h build unchanged from ORIG.Measured: the post's KOI8 example, with its lines ended in 0x0D, throughkoi8-tex.rus gives the post's example.tex byte for byte except for oneleading space on two lines, which the KOI8 input does not have; ALTthrough alt-koi8.rus and then koi8-tex.rus gives the same file.Tables: LIB/translit.  Documents and the plain-text examples: DOC/translit.Build: cc translit.c reg_exp.c reg_sub.c -DOSK